        "body": "For Control Temporary Reporting Access, control 8.12 addresses close with evidence. Require current sources, necessary authority, verified destination state, communication receipt, residual limitation, and named next ownership. Reopen after a material change in identity, scope, policy, system, timing, approval, or source evidence. In this temporary reporting access lane, the reviewer specifically verifies business purpose, report scope, minimum fields, approver, expiry, usage log, and removal evidence, cites the active source version, and records why an unresolved item cannot advance. The retained chronology must distinguish the original instruction from later clarification, coordinator preparation from accountable judgment, and a sent message from verified destination evidence."
