        "body": "For Track Customer Escalation Acknowledgements, control 9.4 addresses separate workflow states. Distinguish intake, evidence collection, exception, owner review, approval, execution, destination verification, communication, and closure. A complete packet is not a decision, an approval is not execution, and a sent notification is not proof that the receiver accepted ownership. In this escalation acknowledgements lane, the reviewer specifically verifies case identity, severity, evidence packet, receiving owner, response clock, acknowledgement, and next action, cites the active source version, and records why an unresolved item cannot advance. The retained chronology must distinguish the original instruction from later clarification, coordinator preparation from accountable judgment, and a sent message from verified destination evidence."
